WEBVTT

00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:16,000
If my oncologist is insisting on chemotherapy and seems to go against everything, I suggest

00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,040
what should I do?

00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:25,280
Well, I would find a different oncologist, you know, it's still a free world and we still

00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:30,480
live in a free health, free world healthcare system.

00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:36,880
I mean, you don't have to stay with who you were initially assigned, assigned.

00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:43,960
So you can even in their old system, let's say you were going to Minnesota oncology or

00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:49,440
you're going to Mayo and you don't like your oncologist, you know, just feel like nothing

00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:56,000
is your suggestions are not being heard, your desires are not being heard.

00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,240
You feel like they just don't really care or you feel like they just, you know, are pushing

00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,200
their agenda, whatever it is, you know, if you don't like me, you don't have to stay with

00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:11,720
me, you don't like your oncologist, go to someone else, there's nothing wrong with

00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,720
that.

00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:17,000
You don't, you're not here to please, some people are such people pleasers, you're afraid

00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,600
you're going to hurt somebody's feelings and then you put your life at risk.

00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:28,520
So don't be foolish, you know, there's lots of oncologists that will take you, especially

00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:33,000
if you go to them and say, hey, I was at Mayo and they were just pushing their agenda,

00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,840
they really want to find somebody that I can work with.

00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:40,160
The next person you talk to will probably be somebody with, I would never do that.

00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:44,000
Oh, no, we can work with you, even though they might have done that to somebody else, you

00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,160
know, two visits before that.

00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:54,440
So just raise your concerns, you know, and, you know, again, like anything, I don't think

00:01:54,440 --> 00:02:01,040
you should be dogmatically positioned either way, I think the best thing is to with a lot

00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:06,640
of prayer and supplication, bring your request made known to God and He will direct your

00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,120
paths and He will give you peace that passes all understanding.

00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:17,480
If you don't have peace about doing a certain therapy that you shouldn't do that therapy, above

00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:23,280
all things, you want to be obedient to what God is leading you to do, not doing something

00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:35,080
to please someone else or doing something to, to a piece of system, and that includes

00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:39,520
not just your, your oncologist includes family members, you have to stand up for what God

00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,200
is telling you to do.

00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:47,840
Years ago, I had a patient that came to me, a pancreatic cancer, late stage, just diagnosed.

00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:52,980
He was doing really well with alternative therapy, about just about a month into care, that's

00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:58,280
who we saw a lot, we had, did a lot of therapies in the office at the time, he was coming in

00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:02,860
every day to do the therapies, he was looking better, his blood work was looking better, and

00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:08,420
his son was just very upset that he was not doing chemotherapy, it was just, it was just

00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:12,820
distraught, that he was not going to do, his dad was not going to do chemotherapy, he thought

00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:17,900
his dad was going to die, if he didn't do chemotherapy, he was just literally having panic attacks.

00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:21,220
And that's what caused the dad to cave, it said, I'm going to go, I just don't think I should

00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,540
do this, but I'm going to go ahead and do it.

00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:28,180
Because I don't just really care, obviously for my son, he did chemotherapy, he died in

00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:36,780
just a couple weeks, I'm convinced of the chemotherapy, he wasn't, his cancer was not progressing,

00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:42,100
the chemotherapy for pancreatic cancer is very severe, and that's one of the main reasons

00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:50,100
I believe that pancreatic cancer patients tend not to survive, do not do things just because

00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:54,740
someone else is pressuring you to do that, no matter if somebody you love or somebody

00:03:54,740 --> 00:04:00,540
you don't know, it's, you do things in anything in life, whether it's making a decision about

00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:05,260
your health care or making a decision about your job, you should be doing things because you're

00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:12,740
consulting by the power of the Holy Spirit, your Heavenly Father, and being obedient to God

00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:19,620
is foremost in having a relationship with God.

00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:27,860
My children will hear my voice, it says, Jesus said, and we need to be listening to it in

00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:33,060
much prayer in all our big life decisions.

00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:39,380
We don't need to spiritualize, you know, whether we should buy butter or the store or something

00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,380
else, but we make it big life decisions.

00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:50,620
These are the things that we are to take to the Lord, and he desires for us to depend on

00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,780
him for those things.

